From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:34:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 092/111] A drag past the end of a line still selects to its
 end

Only the text under the pointer took part in a drag, so dragging past
the end of a line, below a paragraph or beside a table cell dropped the
last characters, and a press in the margin beside the text started
nothing. Now every text run near the pointer reports where the pointer
is nearest in it (the end of a line beside it, its start above it, its
end below it) and the preview keeps the nearest, as a browser does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

